\subsection{Short English statement}
Determine the scope of celestial-mechanics minimization methods across symmetries, topology, masses, stability and fixed-energy constraints.

\subsection{Research attempt}
\paragraph{Model, date and investigated scope.}
OpenAI GPT-6 Astra (configured model \texttt{gpt-6-astra}), ultra reasoning; generated 11 October 2026. Gave explicit mechanical minimality/stability counterchecks and derived traversal-time variation distinguishing fixed period from fixed energy. No general n-body symmetry/topology/mass/stability theory.

\paragraph{Sources and literature check.}
Read the supplied complete definition, catalogue wording, scope qualifications and source list for this canonical ID. The original-source citations are inherited as supplied references; no fresh primary-source or novelty search was performed for this attempt. No current open-status claim is inferred from this calculation.

\paragraph{Action minimality and stability are different.}For the one-dimensional mechanical Lagrangian \(L=\tfrac12\dot x^2+\tfrac12\omega^2x^2\), \(\omega>0\), the zero periodic path is the strict global minimizer among period-P loops: its action is zero and every nonzero loop has positive action. Yet its Euler--Lagrange equation is \(\ddot x=\omega^2x\), whose nonzero solutions grow or decay exponentially; the equilibrium is hyperbolic. Conversely \(L=\tfrac12\dot x^2-\tfrac12\omega^2x^2\) has a linearly stable equilibrium but negative second variation in constant loop directions. These examples show that no generic equivalence between variational minimality and elliptic linear stability is available. They are not Newtonian n-body counterexamples to any specialized theorem.
\paragraph{A fixed-period versus fixed-energy calculation.}For a fixed collision-free geometric loop \(Q(s)\), \(0\le s\le1\), traversed in time \(P\), put \(K_0=\tfrac12\int\sum m_i|Q_i'|^2ds\) and \(U_0=\int U(Q)ds\). Then
\[\mathcal A(P)=K_0/P+PU_0,\qquad \mathcal A'(P)=-K_0/P^2+U_0.
\]
Thus free variation of the traversal time in the ordinary action imposes zero average energy. To target a prescribed energy \(E_*\), the modified functional \(\mathcal A(P)+E_*P\) instead has time stationarity \(K_0/P^2-U_0=E_*\). Fixed-period and fixed-energy minimization are therefore different problems even before collision issues.
\paragraph{Gap.}The source asks for symmetry/topology constraints, arbitrary masses, stability dimensions and usefulness at fixed energy. The calculations only expose two invalid general inferences. A Newtonian theory still needs coercivity, collision avoidance under the actual variations, and a reduced return-map analysis accounting for neutral directions. None is supplied for arbitrary classes or masses; these are the first missing steps before a general description of the method's limits.

\paragraph{Verification and adversarial audit.}
Checked Euler-Lagrange signs, strict periodic minimizer, hyperbolic/elliptic examples and the period-scaling derivative. This was an LLM adversarial audit, not independent human verification; no theorem prover was used. Prompts A then B applied to this ID: Checked Euler-Lagrange signs, strict periodic minimizer, hyperbolic/elliptic examples and the period-scaling derivative. Scope remains limited: Establish Newtonian coercivity and collision avoidance in declared classes, then analyze the symmetry-reduced return map and fixed-energy functional.

Coordinator checked both equilibrium action/stability examples and the period derivatives of the ordinary and prescribed-energy actions. This additional check was model-assisted, not independent human verification.

\paragraph{Tools, process and contributions.}
Python 3 and local shell used to read supplied files and serialize this manuscript; mathematics derived symbolically in the text, with no numerical experiment or formal proof assistant. Contribution prompt A was followed by prompt B. GPT-6 Astra with ultra reasoning drafted the research and performed its stated self-audit; any additional coordinator contribution is identified in the verification and audit. A GPT-6-based Codex coordinator assembled the manuscript and checked repository integration; its exact variant and reasoning configuration were not exposed. No human mathematical contribution, independent human proof check or formal proof certification is supplied. Complete derivations and the consulted source references are included here; private reasoning transcripts are not published.

\paragraph{Final status and first remaining gap.}
\textbf{UNRESOLVED}. Establish Newtonian coercivity and collision avoidance in declared classes, then analyze the symmetry-reduced return map and fixed-energy functional.

